{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include \\\"knn.h\\\"\\n\\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\\n\\n    int i, j, x, y;\\n    int populated = 0;\\n    int ordered = 1;\\n\\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\\n        labels[i] = -1;\\n        distances[i] = -1;\\n    }\\n\\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        Group g = groups[i];\\n\\n        for (j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\\n\\n            /* A full, NaN-free list cannot admit a point at this cutoff. */\\n            if (ordered && populated == k && populated > 0 &&\\n                !(d < distances[populated - 1])) {\\n                continue;\\n            }\\n\\n            /*\\n             * Squared distances never equal the -1 padding sentinel.\\n             * The first unoccupied slot is therefore the default match.\\n             * Reduce integer indices, leaving distance arithmetic scalar.\\n             */\\n            x = populated;\\n#if defined(_OPENMP)\\n#pragma omp simd reduction(min:x)\\n#endif\\n            for (int index = 0; index < populated; index++) {\\n                int candidate = d < distances[index] ? index : populated;\\n                x = candidate < x ? candidate : x;\\n            }\\n\\n            if (x < k) {\\n                /* Copy backward only through occupied entries. */\\n                int last = populated < k ? populated : k - 1;\\n                for (y = last; y > x; y--) {\\n                    distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\\n                    labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\\n                }\\n\\n                distances[x] = d;\\n                labels[x] = g.label;\\n\\n                if (populated < k) {\\n                    populated++;\\n                }\\n\\n                /* Keep exact first-match behavior after storing a NaN. */\\n                if (d != d) {\\n                    ordered = 0;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\\n\\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\\n    int current_frequency = 1;\\n\\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n            }\\n\\n            current_frequency = 1;\\n        } else {\\n            current_frequency++;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    free(distances);\\n    free(labels);\\n    return most_frequent;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\\n    \\n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\\n    }\\n\\n    int k = parse_k();\\n\\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%c\\\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/knn.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"An integer-min reduction exposes SIMD in the neighbor search without changing scalar floating-point distance evaluation. A safe cutoff and occupied-prefix shifts should reduce the remaining serial work.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Unmeasured source-only candidate; no commands executed. Parsing, distance arithmetic, label ordering and voting remain unchanged. Encounter-order cutoff ties and k>N sentinel padding are preserved. No build flags, floating-point modes or thread settings change; worst-case complexity remains O(Nk).\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Replace the early-exit search with a vectorizable minimum-index reduction over occupied distances, with an OpenMP SIMD annotation when OpenMP is enabled.\",\n    \"Reject non-improving points when the neighbor list is full and contains no NaNs; permanently disable this shortcut after storing a NaN.\",\n    \"Shift only occupied entries backward, preserving untouched sentinel padding.\",\n    \"Free per-call neighbor buffers after voting.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
